  "answer": "The conditions required for password cracking, specifically through brute force attacks, include:\n\n1. **Knowledge of the Password Policy**: Understanding the rules governing password creation, such as allowed characters (lowercase letters, uppercase letters, numbers, symbols) and maximum length, is essential to determine the finite space of possible passwords [Source 1].\n\n2. **Access to Password Hashes or Accounts**: Adversaries may need to obtain password hashes or have access to accounts to initiate the cracking process [Source 2].\n\n3. **Account Lockout Policy**: The effectiveness of brute force attacks can be influenced by the account lockout policy in place. A strict account lockout policy can prevent successful brute force attacks by locking accounts after a certain number of failed attempts [Source 3].\n\nThese conditions collectively enable adversaries to systematically guess passwords until they succeed.",
